cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AgentIdeaBench, please cite the paper."
title: "AgentIdeaBench: Benchmarking Scientific Ideation in the Agent Era"
abstract: >-
  Existing benchmarks for scientific hypothesis generation hand a model a curated
  reference set and ask for the paper those references lead to. That static protocol
  has saturated. AgentIdeaBench evaluates the active setting instead, giving a model
  only a subfield name and a literature search tool and letting it choose its own
  retrieval path. Across 40 subfields and 35 models, Active carries 4.4 times the
  between-model variance of Static, and the Active-Static gain is gated by capability.
type: software
license: MIT
